Prefix(:=<http://example.org/forall#>)
Ontology(<http://example.org/forall>
Declaration(Class(:A))
Declaration(Class(:B))
Declaration(Class(:C))
Declaration(Class(:D))
Declaration(ObjectProperty(:r))
# A is everything whose r-successors are all C.
SubClassOf(:A ObjectAllValuesFrom(:r :C))
# B is exactly the things whose r-successors are all (C or D).
EquivalentClasses(:B ObjectAllValuesFrom(:r ObjectUnionOf(:C :D)))
# Entailed: A ⊑ B, because ∀r.C ⊑ ∀r.(C ⊔ D).  Requires the ∀-introduction
# (converse) clause: concluding membership in a universal restriction.
)
